 \Detect it once per 256-byte refill, not once for every buffered OSBGET byte.
 \This remains safe if a loader changes zero-page workspace between refills.
 	JSR	wicfs_detect_machine
+\The MOS zeroes &0780 during a load, which silently disarms the repair helper
+\and leaves the extended-vector table unrepaired from then on. The vectors and
+\the helper therefore restore each other: the helper repairs the table from the
+\BYTEV trap, and this repairs the helper from the vectors, which are reached
+\through the MOS dispatcher and are still working at this point. The check is a
+\single compare, so an intact helper costs nothing.
+	LDA	romsel+(guard_sig-s_guard)
+	CMP	#&A5
+	BEQ	wicfs_guard_present
+	JSR	wicfs_publish_guards_if_host_only
+.wicfs_guard_present
